# gpio-keys.kl — maple hardware keys (Donut 1.6).
# Scancodes from the KitKat port's gpio-keys.kl (yoshino): volume up/down
# plus the two-stage camera key (half press 528, full press 766). POWER
# comes from the separate qpnp_pon device (falls back to qwerty.kl).
# Donut's KeyLayoutMap discards the whole file on an unknown token — keep
# to the Donut KEYCODES/FLAGS sets.
#
# maple has no MENU key and Donut predates on-screen action bars, so the
# camera key's FULL press doubles as MENU (unlocks the keyguard, opens
# app/launcher menus); half press is now BACK for in-app navigation. The
# camera's autofocus (FOCUS) on half-press is given up for this. WAKE_DROPPED
# on the full press mirrors MENU in qwerty.kl (wakes the screen, dropped
# when it woke); the half press does not wake.
key 115   VOLUME_UP         WAKE
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN       WAKE
key 528   BACK
key 766   MENU              WAKE_DROPPED
